# 🌤️ Weather App

A simple React TypeScript weather application that displays real-time weather data, forecasts, and lets users save their favorite locations.

## 🔗 Live Demo
[https://weather-app-7phd.vercel.app](https://weather-app-7phd.vercel.app)

## ✨ Features
- Current weather view (Temperature, Wind Speed, and Conditions)
- Interactive tabs to switch between Hourly and Daily forecasts
- Search bar to look up any city or town
- Save and bookmark favorite locations
- Switch metrics easily between Celsius and Fahrenheit
- Severe weather tracking alerts with browser push notifications
- Full screen error handlers and loading animations
- Fully responsive on mobile layouts

## 🛠️ Tech Stack
- React + TypeScript
- Custom Vanilla CSS (Plain styles, no external CSS frameworks)
- React Router v6
- Axios
- Vite

## 📁 Project Structure
src/
├── Components/
│   ├── Pages/          # Home view dashboard
│   ├── Weather/        # WeatherDisplay, Forecast panels, and Alerts
│   ├── Layout/         # Application Header
│   ├── Settings/       # Simple user preferences screen
│   ├── Button/         # Reusable global button component
│   └── Input/          # Reusable text field component
├── Hooks/              # useWeather and useLocation hooks
├── Types/              # TypeScript types file
├── Utils/              # Notifications background utility
├── App.tsx             # Main router management
└── main.tsx            # Application entrance layout

## 🚀 Installation & Local Setup

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/Thulile18/Weather-App.git

# Enter the project directory
cd Weather-App

# Install student dependencies
npm install

# Start the local development server
npm run dev
```

